{
  "base_commit": "1d4a9bb302f00f72f221dc112592894da482545d",
  "scope": "Entry/results scene native icon/callback access, corrected BG2 screen-base field name and initialization/rendering readability.",
  "changes": [
    "Remove the fake Base virtual view: walk the existing mIcons array through icon_c pointers and call the real virtual Render method, retaining the icon-count reread.",
    "Replace the fake C receiver in scene Render with a dScEntry_c member-pointer type and this receiver; retain an explicitly partial local view for the callback storage at0x64.",
    "Use the existing graphCallback_c fields for its three raw ABI writer helpers, and existing icon_c fields in icon setup. Public helper signatures and names stay unchanged.",
    "Rename graphCallback_c::bg2Priority to bg2ScreenBase: the actual register field supplies the screen address, not the drawing priority.",
    "Use the existing param1 field in InitResources and clarify palette, local-player, icon, screen-map, scale and language-dimension locals. Format the implementations consistently."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "screen_base": "GraphCallback2 clears0x1f00 in register0x0400100c and inserts the field shifted8. The local G2S::GetBG2ScrPtr implementation in src/engine/gx/G2.cpp reads those same bits and uses them to compute the screen address: block<<11 plus0x06200000 in modes0..4, with the documented mode5 branch using<<14 for bitmap mode. Both field accesses and all ten header consumers were checked.",
    "callback_fields": "InitResources passes this to func0211601c with the graph object data0211d71c. The helper stores the scene pointer at+8 and screen base at+0xc. Other writer callers pass the same graph object; func02116030 stores a loaded compressed screen at+4 only when empty. GraphCallback2 consumes/decompresses/deallocates that screen and renders the bound scene icons.",
    "icon_dispatch": "The shared header already owns icon_c mIcons[9], gives icon_c a0x24 extent and declares its virtual Render. Replacing fake method1 dispatch and explicit0x24 byte stepping with this genuine type yields identical complete output. Icon count remains a raw byte at scene+0x280, including its reread after each render.",
    "render_receiver": "The callback view still describes only the existing two-word member-pointer slot at+0x64. Its member-pointer owner is now the actual dScEntry_c receiver. The first-word validity test and pointer-to-slot dispatch shape remain unchanged; this does not claim a complete reconstruction of the surrounding opaque header storage.",
    "ownership": "Queue31 state5803e2a26b3c986b2de0039a344eda7c16202bca had no active owned class/source/header or range conflicts. Edited source ranges in ov075:0x02115ab8..0x02116128,0x0211a26c..0x0211a2b8,0x0211a410..0x0211a734. Header expansion covers ten sources.",
    "runtime_validation": "No new emulator claim: native fields are established by the existing class layouts and direct callers; the corrected register meaning is established by the local SDK reconstruction that computes its screen pointer.",
    "retained_constraints": [
      "Keep shared dThIcon field spellings and its untouched header, scalar Fix12 OAM ABI, volatile xy array, goto arms, width rereads and separate width/height language calls.",
      "Keep local partial render-callback storage, first-word check, raw scene count at0x280, mixed integer/pointer ABI signatures and the remaining opaque entry-scene fields.",
      "Keep source order, destructor/key-function ownership, scene factories, all function/global names, config and production ranges. No new original-TU or full-class reconstruction claim."
    ]
  },
